WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.375
<v Alba>Today, a layout mystery. The page looked perfect in the wireframe.

2
00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:07.586
<v Alba>So why did the footer run away?

3
00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:14.952
<v Alba>Every element is a box. Padding is space inside the border.

4
00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:18.275
<v Alba>Margin is space outside it.

5
00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:21.032
<v Alba>Both are added to each side:

6
00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:26.579
<v Alba>two boxes with 10px margins leave a 20px gap between them.

7
00:00:27.229 --> 00:00:32.103
<v Alba>Four images in an 800px section:

8
00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:41.340
<v Alba>186 + 2×2 border + 2×5 margin = 200px each, 800px in total.

9
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.543
<v Alba>Raise the margin to 10px: 210px each, 840px for four.

10
00:00:46.543 --> 00:00:54.344
<v Alba>The last image drops to a new line, so the page no longer matches its wireframe.

11
00:00:54.994 --> 00:01:00.690
<v Alba>float:left pushes an element to the left, and the content after it wraps around it.

12
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.003
<v Captain>Lieutenant, the footer has run up beside the images!

13
00:01:05.203 --> 00:01:07.856
<v Alba>Floats affect everything after them.

14
00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:11.938
<v Alba>clear:both makes the footer start below every float.

15
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:15.930
<v Alba>Count both sides of the box. Float to line things up.

16
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.198
<v Alba>clear:both to start again below.

